  "headline": "Sekolah Rakyat Program Addresses Out Of School Youth Education",
  "seoTitle": "Sekolah Rakyat Program Addresses Out Of School Youth",
  "metaDescription": "Former workers in Brebes return to education through the Sekolah Rakyat program, as government officials discuss its role in poverty alleviation and SDGs.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Young residents in Brebes have re-enrolled in formal education through the Sekolah Rakyat program after working as domestic helpers.",
    "The Sekolah Rakyat initiative is being expanded across various regions, including new land preparation in Temanggung and ongoing sites in Kediri.",
    "Government officials and stakeholders are highlighting the program as a key mechanism for poverty alleviation and achieving sustainable development goals."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Sekolah Rakyat program is gaining national attention as an alternative educational model aimed at providing opportunities for out-of-school youth and individuals seeking to improve their prospects. Recently, the initiative gained prominence in Brebes, where young workers transitioned from domestic labor to resume their studies. The program is part of broader government efforts to tackle poverty and support the achievement of Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). Development of the initiative continues, with local governments, such as those in Temanggung, dedicating space for new centers. Meanwhile, other regions like Kediri have reported on the diverse roles supporting students, such as specialized care providers. Officials, including representatives from Bappenas and the Ministry of Social Affairs, have emphasized the distinction between this model and conventional schools, advocating for its role in addressing hunger and academic accessibility for underprivileged children.",
